ls.","published":"2026-11-16T00:22:20.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50495687/sooners-boosted-crowd-ire-postponement-beat-rebels","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Mark Schlabach","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2026 college football SP+ rankings for all 138 FBS teams","description":"The updated SP+ rankings, plus strength of schedule and résumé SP+, after this weekend's results.","published":"2026-11-15T22:56:34.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/49868647/2026-college-football-sp+-rankings-all-138-fbs-teams","type":"Story","byline":"Bill Connelly","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Sizing up college football's best races down the homestretch","description":"From spots in the CFP and SEC title game to the hunt for bowl eligibility, there's still a lot on the line.","published":"2026-11-15T22:17:31.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50491637/connelly-college-football-best-races","type":"Story","byline":"Bill Connelly","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"SEC fines Arkansas $500K for allowing fans to storm field vs. South Carolina","description":"The Southeastern Conference fined Arkansas $500,000 on Sunday for allowing fans to storm the field following a 34-6 victory over No. 17 South Carolina.","published":"2026-11-15T22:01:10.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50493903/sec-fines-arkansas-500k-allowing-fans-storm-field-vs-south-carolina","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Clemson QB Tait Reynolds has torn meniscus, Christopher Vizzina a concussion","description":"Clemson lost starting QB Tait Reynolds for the rest of the season with a torn meniscus, while backup Christopher Vizzina has a concussion.","published":"2026-11-15T21:09:56.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50493355/reynolds-torn-meniscus-vizzina-concussion","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Andrea Adelson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Minnesota fires OC Greg Harbaugh Jr., ending third stint with Gophers","description":"Minnesota fired offensive coordinator Greg Harbaugh Jr. as the Golden Gophers rank 15th in the Big Ten in scoring and 17th in yards per game.","published":"2026-11-15T19:36:27.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50491908/minnesota-fires-oc-greg-harbaugh-jr-ending-3rd-gophers-stint","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Jake Trotter","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Allstate Playoff Predictor","description":"Select your favorite contender, make your picks for how its season will play out and see what the Allstate Playoff Predictor foretells.","published":"2026-11-15T18:13:44.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/feature/story/_/page/cfbplayoffpredictor/college-football-allstate-playoff-bracket-predictor","type":"Eticket","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2027 NFL draft questions, latest intel, risers, CFB standouts","description":"Is Jackson Harris the WR3 in the class? And has Boubacar Traore emerged as the No. 3 edge rusher? Here's our weekly draft spin, including top standouts.","published":"2026-11-15T17:34:06.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/draft2027/story/_/id/49881131/2027-nfl-draft-risers-questions-college-football-prospects","type":"Story","byline":"Mel Kiper Jr. and Jordan Reid","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5079426/wendell-gregory","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wendell_Gregory"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Wendell Gregory","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wendell_Gregory","description":"American football player (born 2006)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:37:24Z","intro":"Wendell J. Gregory (born January 27, 2006) is an American college football defensive end for the Kansas State Wildcats. He previously played for the South Carolina Gamecocks and Oklahoma State Cowboys.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Gregory is from Marietta, Georgia. He attended George Walton Comprehensive High School in Marietta where he played football, initially as a wide receiver before moving to linebacker as a sophomore. Across his sophomore and junior seasons, he tallied 86 tackles, 11 tackles-for-loss (TFLs), 5.5 sacks and two interceptions. He then had 56 tackles, 18 TFLs and seven sacks as a senior in 2023, helping Walton to a record of 14–1 with an appearance in the 7A state championship. A four-star recruit, Gregory was ranked by 247Sports as the 12th-best linebacker prospect and the 130th-best player nationally in the recruiting class of 2024. He committed to play college football for the South Carolina Gamecocks."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"As a true freshman at South Carolina in 2024, Gregory appeared in two games and redshirted, posting a tackle, while playing as a defensive end. He entered the NCAA transfer portal after the season and transferred to the Oklahoma State Cowboys. He became a starter for the Cowboys in 2025. Through nine games, he was the leader among FBS freshmen with 10.5 tackles-for-loss. He was named a semifinalist for the Shaun Alexander Freshman of the Year award."}]}}